    "run_views_mentions_refit": true,
    "run_views_refit_uses_all_rows_heuristic": false,
    "full_refit_would_use_fraction": 1.0,
    "note": "A second-pass refit on all labelled rows is the documented test-time policy, so a submitted model is already trained on 100% of the labels. The CV-stage OOF numbers, by contrast, come from models that saw only the outer-fit fraction reported above. That asymmetry is the reason OOF and test-time behaviour differ, and it is why the honest way to improve test performance is NOT to train the fold models on more data -- they already cannot be, the held-out fold is what makes their OOF score meaningful -- but to make sure the refit iteration count is chosen without using any held-out information."
